{
  "description": "Version reporting to the Supertext Commando Center, the automatic API key check and the callback ping (protocol: Commando-Center-Supertext-Translation → docs/DEVELOPER.md → Report protocol; its spec/ files are copied to spec/commando/). 'fingerprint': SHA-256 (lower-case hex) of the key as authHeader() would send it (trimmed, a pasted 'Supertext-Auth-Key ' prefix removed); '' for a blank key. 'apiKeyCheck': how the answer to GET features (10 s timeout, the usual 429 retries) becomes a check: 2xx ok, 401/403 invalid, 5xx or no HTTP answer unreachable, anything else error; httpStatus is the status (null without an answer), errorCode the body's JSON error_code (null if none, at most 100 characters). A blank key gives missing without a request. 'enabled': the reporting setting (null = not set, default on) and SUPERTEXT_VERSION_REPORTS (0/false/off/no turns it off, 1/true/on/yes on, anything else or unset leaves the setting). 'ping': the answer of the plugin's ping endpoint (JSON body compared parsed; headers Content-Type: application/json and Cache-Control: no-store on every answer). 'scenarios': the reporter's state machine. The state is a JSON object the plugin stores as it is: reportedVersions ('<plugin>|<system>|<runtime>' versions last reported, missing parts empty), reportedKeyStatus (key status last reported), lastFailureAt (time of the last failed report), keyCheck (the latest check with the key's fingerprint). Times are UTC ISO 8601 without fractions ('2026-10-13T08:00:00Z'). Actions: afterSettingsSaved (always checks the key; reports installed if never reported, else settings_saved); onRequest (checks the key only if its fingerprint differs from keyCheck's; then reports installed if never reported, upgraded if the versions changed, api_key_check if the key status differs from reportedKeyStatus, else nothing); authenticationFailed (sets the check to invalid with the given HTTP status, no request to Supertext, then like onRequest); testConnection (always checks the key, then like onRequest); reportCheck (always sends event check, ignoring the throttle). Reports go only when reporting is enabled and not within 3600 s after lastFailureAt (except reportCheck). A report is sent when the center answers 2xx; then reportedVersions and reportedKeyStatus are updated and lastFailureAt cleared; otherwise only lastFailureAt is set to now. The report body: schema 1, event, site_url, plugin, system, runtime, sdk_version, api_key_configured (fingerprint not empty), api_key_check (status, checked_at, http_status and error_code when set), callback.url when a callback URL is configured; fields compared parsed. A step's 'features' and 'report' are the answers to GET features and POST report (status and body, or transportError); 'requests' lists which were made, in order.",
  "defaults": {
    "reportUrl": "https://commandocenter-production.up.railway.app/api/v1/report",
    "reportTimeoutSeconds": 3,
    "keyCheckTimeoutSeconds": 10,
    "failureBackoffSeconds": 3600
  },
